invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: diff_p256_wide
reason: the conversion back from Jacobian coordinates builds the move's
  mask from X where it reads Z. At (0 : 0 : 0) X is zero too, so the
  point at infinity p256_wide_mul holds still comes out right, and every
  point at infinity bin/p256_equiv_test converts has X zero or a Y that
  is not: that test passes. bin/diff_p256_wide converts (X : 0 : 0) for a
  random X against spec/lean/Spec/P256WidePoint.lean's fromJacobian,
  which moves 1 into Y there, where this file leaves 0.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_cmov(&o->y, &p256_wide_fe_one_mont, p256_wide_fe_zero_mask(&a->z));
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_cmov(&o->y, &p256_wide_fe_one_mont, p256_wide_fe_zero_mask(&a->x));
